# One compiler-fuzzing campaign, as a standalone child-process entry, for running from SOURCE: compiler-hunt.tree
# spawns this module's emitted port, the sibling of its own, under tsx. The built CLI does not use it: it carries
# `run-fuzz-campaign` in its own bundle and forks itself, because a file beside the running module does not exist
# inside host/line.js.
#
# Usage (spawned, not run by hand): tsx fuzz-entry.ts <report-out> <probe-file> <runs> <seed> [<corpus.json>] [<budget>]
#
# Ported from deck/test/code/fuzz-campaign.ts (term-cli-in-term-0110), which compiler-fuzz.ts's original ran.

load ./compiler-fuzzing
  find run-fuzz-campaign

bind campaign-arguments
  like list, like text
  case node
    text <process.argv.slice(2)>

host campaign-report, run-fuzz-campaign(campaign-arguments())
